{"abstract":"Ultrasound is essential in fetal medicine for diagnosing and monitoring, but it requires extensive training. Artificial intelligence (AI) shows a great promise in enhancing the clinical training and practice, by improving workflow and standardising diagnostics. Despite its potential, AI's limitations and regulatory challenges must be addressed before full integration. Research should focus on implementation to achieve successful use in clinical practice. Ultimately, AI is expected to support clinicians rather than replace them, improving diagnostic accuracy and efficiency in fetal medicine.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Taksøe-Vester, Caroline","Bashir, Zahra","Sejer, Emilie Pi Fogtmann","Ngo, Mary Le","Pedersen, Lars Henning","Friis, Mikkel","Petersen, Olav B.","Feragen, Aasa","Nielsen, Mads","Christensen, Anders Nymark","Tolsgaard, Martin G."],"cuid":["S03-091.71-813483"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Taksøe-Vester, Caroline"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Female","Humans","Pregnancy","Ultrasonography Prenatal"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kunstig intelligens og føtalmedicinsk ultralydskanning","src":["aau","au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V10240748","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-091.71-813483","identifier":[{"id":"40358082","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005377863","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e2dd8dd0-ae99-4b67-948e-570986a9efba"